{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794857793757271406,"compiled_state":{"alias":"almondy-columned-iguanodon","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fe863af846e4db29f7a496ac7ca3b4c98dcadba546ea2b0c6803a01665e04499","event_uuid":"c5c156dd-a2d8-4abf-9eeb-8afa1b7b374a","position":{"commit_sha":"463ba4b7121b42ca24ff4f79dc2bd911988909ce","position":"1794857635742574816-c5c156dd-a2d8-4abf-9eeb-8afa1b7b374a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"587cf8cde6e4c39bc1000ac3b424f2a56d13f6e6c1471a94f4e2ea776864c1f0","event_uuid":"dec44873-0151-41ca-a9ee-95eac294f206","position":{"commit_sha":"45bcfc93064f6dc5837334173faf9ee574ed39b8","position":"1794857727832228439-dec44873-0151-41ca-a9ee-95eac294f206"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c7bd45fa2fd91ed07998cccd644ef46cad6d8bcbb657d55bd3ab570854ed56f3","event_uuid":"2ca62077-acd0-43a8-bb9d-2c8ce2693cc9","position":{"commit_sha":"74761dff1b66066e0a956ff650566aa2a0a49e0b","position":"1794857793757271405-2ca62077-acd0-43a8-bb9d-2c8ce2693cc9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794857635742574816,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dec44873-0151-41ca-a9ee-95eac294f206","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"2ca62077-acd0-43a8-bb9d-2c8ce2693cc9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"47d8-baf8-2348-45c9"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job runs a maintained subset held green: tests known to fail on Windows are deselected through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-permissions.args`. This bug owns that file: 47 tests in 8 modules, from the 5 scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16).\n\nThe op-cert key loader (`rebar.opcert_service.keyprov`) requires mode `0600 or stricter`, and `cleanup_comment_echo_jira` requires its artifact directory not be group/world accessible. Windows reports `0o666`/`0o777` because it does not implement POSIX mode bits. The policy question of whether rebar owes an ACL equivalent on Windows is task cloistered-decomposed-nymph.\n\nModules: `tests/integration/test_cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py` (17), `tests/unit/test_opcert_service.py` (12), `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py` (5), `tests/unit/test_rp04_s6_opcert_startup.py` (5), `tests/unit/test_opcert_key_copy_leak_tortoise.py` (4), `tests/unit/test_mcp_drain_signing_iguanodon.py` (2), `tests/unit/test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py` (1), `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_integrity.py` (1).\n\nExample: `OpcertKeyError: REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH='C:\\...' ... 0600 or stricter (group/other bits set: mode 0o666)`.\n\n## Approach\n\nFollow the decision on cloistered-decomposed-nymph: either skip the mode check where the platform does not honour POSIX bits (with a test that pins that branch), or implement an ACL check.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe failing product or test code for this class, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-permissions.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Testing\n\nPOSIX: the touched tests still pass under `make verify`. Windows: a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change passes with the removed lines no longer deselected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-permissions.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","47d8-baf8-2348-45c9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"44b2-e70e-2b9f-4d2a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: POSIX mode-bit checks reject keys and artifact dirs on Windows (47 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c5c156dd-a2d8-4abf-9eeb-8afa1b7b374a","dec44873-0151-41ca-a9ee-95eac294f206","2ca62077-acd0-43a8-bb9d-2c8ce2693cc9"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794857793757271406,"uuid":"008a14c5-43bd-4c9c-9439-3d94230853fd"}
